    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_048a60b3e87534a7d8faf102788b230e3daa8d70ec383e1595f8a357bfda9476",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "The explicit primorial sequence is a countertest for extending Theorem 7's stronger totient inequality to all even integers. Nicolas's cited dichotomy makes the obstruction unavoidable: under RH every primorial has n/φ(n)>e^γ log log n, while if RH is false infinitely many primorials still do. Thus this uniform strengthening cannot be the route to the even case, although this says nothing against Robin's original inequality or other proof strategies.",
