    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_59a543c9d66d92de26de2b7df9325fa6a9a7fa384c7a3c907d5d72199dbfa898",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "For every fixed exponent cap t, the t-free limsup of sigma(n)/(n log log n) loses the Euler-product factor 1/zeta(t), and uniform exponent-(t-1) prime products attain that bound. Hence an infinite sequence of Robin failures cannot remain in any fixed t-free class: under the source's false-RH consequence, its maximum prime exponent must tend to infinity.",
