      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_786fc37e32e11b73590f21d869922fe8ee77b86f6fdf24908a200628b33ee4c4",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "For a least 5-free Robin failure above 5040, deletion of the largest prime forces P(n)<log n; explicit truncated Euler-product control then bootstraps that inequality to P(n)<=73. Exponent-pattern canonicalization reduces the remaining case either to the finitely verified Hardy-Ramanujan family or to a separate bounded small-representative branch, both of which the source reports checking computationally.",
